            <title>[LU-20980] lnetctl net show dump size wraps u16 min_dump_alloc with 8+ NIs</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20980</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt; &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20221" title="LNet: lnet_net_show_dump NULL pointer dereference during multi-skb netlink dumps" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20221"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20221&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (b94f56769f) sizes the lnetctl net show dump buffer per NI and writes the total into cb-&amp;gt;min_dump_alloc. On kernels where that field is u16, the total wraps once it passes 65535. At ~6.5KB per NI, 0@lo plus 8 tcp NIs gives 66162, which wraps to 626. That is smaller than the U16_MAX it replaced.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  Two smaller problems are in the same code:&lt;br/&gt;
▎ - lnet_net_size_skb() resets prev_type from its LNET_NET_ANY argument rather than the net being sized, so it charges a key table for every net.&lt;br/&gt;
▎ - The malformed-request exit in lnet_net_show_start() returns without freeing nlist. -&amp;gt;done() is not called when -&amp;gt;start() fails.&lt;br/&gt;
▎&lt;br/&gt;
▎ Fix: Sum into a local ssize_t and cap at the field's maximum, as lnet_route_show_start() does. This keeps large nodes at the old U16_MAX instead of making net show fail. Also track prev_type correctly and take the malformed-request exit through report_err.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
